  "summary": "0087C640 the parent-most (damageable) class constructor, so descriptor +0h..+6Bh is attributed; 00837DE0 the session-mode-dependent gameplay-settings tuning block selector; and the eight per-ship-class leaf overrides of descriptor vtable slot +8h, whose class names were recovered from the literal after each leaf vtable. 006FE6A0 MDestroyer reads no Lua key at all: its +560h..+570h writes are copies out of the settings block. 00960230 and 00831840 were already decoded in docs/VEHICLE_CLASS_FIELDS.md and docs/SHIP_CLASS_FIELDS.md and are not repeated.",
  "corrections": [
    {
      "target": "006FE6A0",
      "was": "docs/VEHICLE_CLASS_DESCRIPTORS.md line 235: the MDestroyer override of slot +8h 'writes +560h..+570h', listed alongside the Lua field readers",
      "is": "006FE6A0 opens no LuaObject and reads no key. After chaining to 00831840 it calls 00424C40 then 00837DE0 twice and copies two dwords out of the returned tuning block into +560h..+56Ch and +570h",
      "evidence": "the whole body 006FE6A0-006FE6EC: no SEH frame, no 00B678xx call, MOV EAX,[EAX+0Ch] at 006FE6B9 and MOV ECX,[EAX+8] at 006FE6E0"
    },
    {
      "target": "00854230 SwimDepth1",
      "was": "SwimDepth1 reads as a field of its own alongside SwimDepth2 and SwimDepth3",
      "is": "SwimDepth1 writes the same slot +810h as PeriscopeDepth and is read only when PeriscopeDepth left it negative; it is the legacy alias, not a second field",
      "evidence": "XORPS XMM0,XMM0 / COMISS XMM0,[ESI+810h] / JBE 00854378 at 00854332"
    }
  ],
